{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Remediation for Gerrit change 2984 ps8 blocking finding completed in worktree fix-terraform-drift-8d27. `_metered_spend` now keeps the existing `float | None` convention but reserves `None` for real CloudWatch backend failures; a no-per-model-series quiet day returns `0.0`, so the main gate treats it as an available zero-spend signal and can release existing restrictions while still refusing release on genuine signal outage. Added/updated handler tests for quiet-day release, first-trip SNS, release SNS, and the no-usable-series unit expectation. Evidence: RED quiet-day test failed with `assert True is False` and `metered_status=unavailable`; focused file `49 passed`; handler coverage `305 stmts, 0 miss, 120 branches, 0 partial, 100%`; `make lint` passed. Teeth checks failed as intended for quiet-day release, trip SNS subject, and release SNS subject. Amended commit: 4417645d25a1b98a9fd46214589dedf23c551c5a. Not pushed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789782579565543083,"uuid":"0d18ef8a-5f9a-47d3-9972-a54d23c9a6af"}